1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,110
Listen to a talk in a literature class.

2
00:00:03,110 --> 00:00:07,140
Woman: A common theme in literature is isolation

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:09,140
and that's what we'll explore today.

4
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:11,920
Isolation can be a powerful motif

5
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:15,220
reflecting the psychological effects of being separated from society.

6
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:20,260
One of the most classic examples of isolation in literature is Mary Shelley's Frankenstein.

7
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:24,014
In this novel, Victor Frankenstein's grotesque creation - the creature -

8
00:00:24,014 --> 00:00:28,980
experiences profound isolation due to his monstrous appearance

9
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:30,270
and the fear he instills in people.

10
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:34,587
This isolation leads to anger and a desire for revenge,

11
00:00:34,587 --> 00:00:38,040
thus highlighting the detrimental effects of being ostracized.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,090
Another notable example is The Catcher in the Rye by J. D. Salinger.

13
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:46,484
The protagonist Holden Caulfield feels disconnected from the world around him,

14
00:00:46,484 --> 00:00:49,280
and he struggles with alienation and loneliness.

15
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,100
This social isolation is what drives Holden's actions

16
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,240
and internal conflicts throughout the book.

17
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:58,320
Yet another example of isolation in literature

18
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:02,010
and one that ends badly, is Herman Melville's Moby-Dick.

19
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:04,560
In this novel, Captain Ahab's obsessive

20
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:08,030
vengeful quest for the white whale leads to his isolation.

21
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:11,254
This obsession distances him from his crew as well as his humanity,

22
00:01:11,254 --> 00:01:14,210
and it propels him and his ship toward a destructive end.

23
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:18,150
However, the portrayal of isolation in literature is not always negative.

24
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:20,480
In Charlotte Brontë's Jane Eyre

25
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:24,220
the titular character experiences isolation at various points in her life.

26
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:27,509
For example, when she is sent to live with her unkind relatives,

27
00:01:27,509 --> 00:01:30,250
and later when she experiences loneliness at a boarding school.

28
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:36,060
But Jane is resilient in the face of isolation, becoming strong and independent.
